# DocAgent API: one request for every endpoint (guide 1 §4.4).
# Start the AppHost first, then run the requests from top to bottom: later requests use the ids of earlier ones.
# VS Code: the REST Client extension ("Send Request" above each request). Visual Studio: built in.
#
# The upload carries a tiny synthetic pack inline. When Darko's packs are in samples/, upload one of those instead:
#   < ../../samples/<system>/<variant>/<file>   (paths are relative to this file)

@api = https://localhost:7133

### What can a run be made of? The templates...
GET {{api}}/api/templates

### ...and the strategies, grouped by slot (all fakes for now)
GET {{api}}/api/strategies

### Create a run with explicit strategy keys. Answers 202 with the run id.
# @name createRun
POST {{api}}/api/runs
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=DocAgentPack

--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="templateId"

system-assessment
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="detector"

rules
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="author"

single-agent
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="retrieval"

tool
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="brief"

Describe the field service system before we integrate it.
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="data/work_orders.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

id,technician_id,customer_id,status,opened_at
WO-1001,T-07,C-311,open,2026-10-01
WO-1002,T-09,C-118,closed,2026-10-02
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="openapi.yaml"
Content-Type: application/yaml

openapi: 3.0.3
info:
  title: Helio Service API
  version: "2.4"
paths:
  /work-orders:
    get:
      summary: List work orders
--DocAgentPack--

### Poll the run: send this again until status is Completed (about 3 seconds with the fakes)
GET {{api}}/api/runs/{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}

### Or watch the progress as Server-Sent Events (REST Client shows them when the stream ends)
GET {{api}}/api/runs/{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}/events

### The SystemModel behind the design
GET {{api}}/api/runs/{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}/model

### The design as a Markdown download
GET {{api}}/api/runs/{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}/design.md

### Rerun on the same files with another author. Fields left out keep the source run's values.
# @name rerun
POST {{api}}/api/runs/{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}/rerun
Content-Type: application/json

{ "author": "specialists" }

### The rerun: sourceRunId points back at the first run
GET {{api}}/api/runs/{{rerun.response.body.$.runId}}

### The latest runs, filtered by author
GET {{api}}/api/runs?author=specialists

### Feedback on one section: 1 is good, -1 is bad. Answers 204.
POST {{api}}/api/runs/{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 1, "sectionId": "data-model", "comment": "Clear and complete." }

### Ask about the run. The answer streams as Server-Sent Events; the conversation id is in the X-Conversation-Id header.
# @name ask
POST {{api}}/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "runId": "{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}", "question": "Which entities did you find?" }

### A follow-up in the same conversation: the first question and answer are now its history
POST {{api}}/api/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "runId": "{{createRun.response.body.$.runId}}", "conversationId": "{{ask.response.headers.X-Conversation-Id}}", "question": "Which of them are risky?" }

### Add a knowledge document (our own words, so licence "internal"). Answers 202.
POST {{api}}/api/knowledge
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=DocAgentKnowledge

--DocAgentKnowledge
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

Pattern
--DocAgentKnowledge
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="license"

internal
--DocAgentKnowledge
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="outbox-pattern.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

# Outbox pattern

Write the change and the event to publish in one database transaction, then publish from the outbox table.
--DocAgentKnowledge--

### Search the knowledge base (debug)
GET {{api}}/api/knowledge/search?q=file feed&kind=Pattern&top=3

### A bad request on purpose: unknown template and strategy. Answers 400 with the problems per field.
POST {{api}}/api/runs
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=DocAgentPack

--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="templateId"

no-such-template
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="author"

magentic
--DocAgentPack
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="a.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

id
1
--DocAgentPack--
